    lessonText: "Two weeks in the Word. Take inventory again.\n\nYou know what the Bible is and why it can be trusted — not just by faith, but by evidence. You have a method for reading it: what does it say, what does it mean, what do I do? You understand the relationship between the Old and New Testaments. You know that doubt is not disqualifying and that perseverance in the habit matters more than any single session.\n\nMost importantly, you have been in the Word for 30 days. That is not nothing. Thirty days of 10-minute seeds in the ground. They are growing whether you can see it or not.\n\nHebrews 11:1 is your verse to carry forward. Faith is not certainty about outcomes — it is confidence in the Person who holds all outcomes.",
