    lessonText: "Prayer is not a spiritual performance. It is a conversation with your Father — the same Father who already knows what you need before you ask. So why pray? Because prayer is not primarily about giving God information. It is about relationship.\n\n1 Thessalonians 5:17 says \"pray without ceasing\" — which cannot mean stay on your knees 24 hours a day. It means cultivate an orientation of prayer. An ongoing awareness of God's presence.\n\nThe Lord's Prayer is a template, not a script. Jesus gave it as a framework: acknowledge who God is, invite His kingdom, ask for what you need, deal with forgiveness, ask for protection. It covers all of human need in about 60 words.",
