    scriptureText: "Likewise the Spirit also helpeth our infirmities: for we know not what we should pray for as we ought: but the Spirit itself maketh intercession for us with groanings which cannot be uttered.",
    lessonText: "There are moments when you don't know what to pray. The situation is too complex, the pain too deep, the future too uncertain. You have words, but they feel insufficient for the weight of what you're carrying.\n\nRomans 8:26 is the promise for exactly those moments: the Spirit intercedes for you with groanings that cannot be expressed in words. The Holy Ghost takes what your words cannot carry and carries it for you before God.\n\nJude 1:20 tells believers to build themselves up by praying in the Holy Ghost. This is the tongues prayer — the prayer that bypasses your reasoning mind and comes from the deepest part of your spirit. Paul says in 1 Corinthians 14:4 that the one who prays in tongues \"edifies himself\" — builds himself up.",
