    lessonText: "God inhabits the praises of His people — not just your personal praise, but the collective voice of a congregation worshipping together. There is something that happens in the gathered worship of a church that cannot happen in your living room alone.\n\nHebrews 13:15 calls it the \"sacrifice of praise.\" Sacrifice because it costs something — it requires you to put aside your circumstances and offer your praise regardless. The word \"continually\" means this is not reserved for good days.\n\nWhen you walk into Elkhart Life Church on Sunday and the congregation lifts their voices together, you are joining something ancient and powerful. You are adding your voice to a sound that reaches heaven. Don't sit it out.",
