    scriptureText: "But if ye forgive not men their trespasses, neither will your Father forgive your trespasses. — And be ye kind one to another, tenderhearted, forgiving one another, even as God for Christ's sake hath forgiven you.",
    lessonText: "Jesus makes forgiveness bilateral in Matthew 6: the way you forgive others is directly connected to the forgiveness you receive. Unforgiveness keeps a door closed in your own heart that God is trying to walk through.\n\nForgiveness does not mean what happened was acceptable. It does not require reconciliation in every case. Forgiveness is the release of the debt — \"I am no longer holding this against you before God.\" It frees the forgiver more than the forgiven.\n\nEphesians 4:32 gives the model and the motivation in one sentence: forgive as God for Christ's sake has forgiven you. The standard is what God did for you — completely, at great cost, when you did not deserve it.",
