    lessonText: "Many people find it easier to forgive others than to receive forgiveness for themselves. They confess, receive, then return to carrying the guilt anyway — as if God's forgiveness wasn't quite enough for what they did.\n\n1 John 1:9 is a promise with two parts: God will forgive and He will cleanse. Not just pardon — cleanse. The record is wiped, the residue is removed. And it is based not on the quality of your confession but on His faithfulness.\n\nPsalm 103:12 puts a distance on it: as far as the east is from the west. That is not a finite distance. East and west do not converge — they are infinitely opposed directions. That is how far God removes your sin when you confess it.",
