    lessonText: "1 Corinthians 10:13 contains one of the most practical promises in all of Scripture: every temptation has a way of escape. God builds the exit before He allows the entrance. Your job is to look for the exit, not to stand there fascinated with the entrance.\n\nJames 4:7 gives you two actions: \"Submit yourselves therefore to God. Resist the devil, and he will flee from you.\" Both are required. Submit is an active choice to align yourself under God's authority. Resist is confrontation, pushback, refusal.\n\nYou will be tempted. Every Christian is. The goal is not to never be tempted — it is to develop the reflexes to respond correctly when you are.",
