    lessonText: "Proverbs 18:21 is blunt: your tongue carries the power of death and life, and you will eat the fruit of what you speak. What comes out of your mouth is not neutral — it is seed that produces a harvest.\n\nJames 3 is one of the most extended treatments of the tongue in Scripture. He compares it to a ship's rudder — a small thing that determines the direction of the whole vessel. With the same tongue we bless God and curse people. He calls this absurd.\n\nBecoming a Christian does not automatically clean up your speech. That is a discipline. It requires intentionality about what you say, how you say it, and what you say about others when they are not in the room.",
