    scriptureText: "Moreover if thy brother shall trespass against thee, go and tell him his fault between thee and him alone. — If it be possible, as much as lieth in you, live peaceably with all men.",
    lessonText: "Jesus did not leave conflict resolution vague. Matthew 18:15-17 gives specific steps: go to the person directly, alone, first. Not to mutual friends. Not to the whole church. Directly, privately, first.\n\nRomans 12:18 adds a qualifier: \"as much as lieth in you\" — meaning you cannot control the outcome, but you can control your part. You can choose not to escalate. You can choose to go first.\n\nConflict handled biblically is one of the clearest proofs of Christian maturity. Anyone can avoid confrontation or weaponize it. It takes genuine character to go directly, humbly, and honestly to the person involved.",
